/*  EXPECTED: COMPILES and runs; compiled output must match the interpreter.

    A helper puts a text key and a text value it makes into the map it is given.

    A text is never refused; one stored where a body cannot see how long the target lives is
    copied, when the program runs, into the region the target itself lives in (docs/SOUNDNESS.md,
    obligation O4). */

Bind void to note-it, given (the map from text to text notes):
    In notes, the entry for ("k" joined to "1") becomes "v" joined to "1".
Done.
Define notes as a map from text to text.
Pull a rabbit.
    Cast note-it on (notes).
Done.

Define churn as a series of text.
Define tick as 0.
While tick is less than 400, repeat:
    Insert ("zzzzzzzz" joined to "yyyyyyyy") into churn.
    tick becomes tick + 1.
Done.
State the entry for "k1" in notes but void is "none".
